# Yatra.AI — Wireframes

> Designing the end-to-end experience for an AI-orchestrated group travel platform.

This folder contains the **low-fidelity wireframes** created for Yatra.AI, a multi-agent travel planning product designed to simplify the fragmented group-travel journey — from trip initiation and preference collection to collaborative decisions, budgeting, booking, in-trip support, and post-trip engagement.

The wireframes were created before the high-fidelity prototype to validate **user experience, navigation flow, information architecture, and task progression** before investing in visual design.

## 🎯 UX Objectives

- Reduce planning effort and cognitive load
- Make group decision-making easier
- Make AI recommendations transparent and understandable
- Keep users in control of important decisions
- Create a predictable end-to-end travel flow
- Connect planning, booking, travel support, and post-trip engagement

## 🧭 UX Principles

| Principle | Design Intent |
|---|---|
| **WhatsApp-First** | Minimize onboarding friction by starting the journey through an existing communication platform. |
| **Progressive Disclosure** | Show only the information needed at each stage. |
| **Collaborative Decision Making** | Help groups compare preferences, resolve conflicts, and reach consensus. |
| **Trust & Transparency** | Provide visible decision checkpoints, pricing information, and human approval before major commitments. |
| **Reduced Cognitive Load** | Break complex travel planning into simple, guided steps supported by AI. |
| **Consistent Navigation** | Maintain predictable information hierarchy and interaction patterns. |

